<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68782" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόρσῐμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόρος</span>) poet. Adj., used also
		by <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
		</span></i>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>appointed by fate,
				destined</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ δέ κ᾽ ἔπειτα γήμαιθ᾽ ὅς κε πλεῖστα
					πόροι καὶ μόρσιμος ἔλθοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					16.392
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἄρ᾽ Ὀδυσσῆϊ . . μόρσιμον ἦεν
					. . Διὸς υἱὸν ἀποκτάμεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.674
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἐστι θεῷ . . δαμῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					19.417
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.154
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾧ θανεῖν οὐ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					933
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοὶ μὲν γαμεῖσθαι μ. γαμεῖν δ᾽ ἐμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					13
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μόρσιμον</span>
			<i>destiny, doom</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				12.30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				263
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				282
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				236
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				953
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μόρσιμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sol.
					13.55
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>foredoomed to die</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔ τοι μόρσιμός εἰμι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.13
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόρσιμον ἦμαρ</span> the day
				<i>of doom</i>, <i><span class="en">
				15.613
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.175
			</span></i>; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. αἰών</span> one's
				<i>appointed</i> time, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				2.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				46
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
